  "title": "Mosaic spaces generated by continua and by Peano continua",
  "abstract": "Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of an article on Davison's mosaic spaces and three questions recorded by Lavallee (1964). Formalized: every theorem, lemma, proposition and corollary of Sections 2, 4, 6 and 7 and the classical facts they use (abstract Definition 2.1 and its equivalence with the intrinsic definition; the arc theorem; compact locally connected metrizable spaces are locally path connected; Proposition 2.10 on path-determined spaces), the space G (Tychonoff, locally arcwise connected, not a quasi-curve space), the cone construction, boundary bumping (Lemma 5.2), and the answers to all three questions: Q3 by G, Q2 and Q1a/Q1b by the cone over G. Not formalized (examples, excluded by the author's request): Section 3 and the Appendix (the space E(K)), van Douwen's space in Section 5, Example 7.3 (cZ) and the strictness claims of Theorem 7.4 that use them; also the Hahn-Mazurkiewicz theorem, which no formalized result needs.",
